d umbilical cord if you  happen to have gotten all three of these  you only need three to trigger the event  however there is a fourth one in case  you missed one of these the fourth is a  little trickier to get as it comes from  another npc named Ariana after defeating  vicar Amelia make your way to the  streets to the side of the cathedral  pass the flamethrower guy proceeded down  the street and head left toward a door  with a red lantern and talked to a young  lady talk to her a second time to tell  her it's safe to go to the cathedral  ward if you haven't triggered the  ability to send people to the cathedral  ward make sure to talk to Owen chapel  door will then give you the ability to  do so  now that you saved Ariana you can leave  her be for now after defeating her go to  wet-nurse  head back to the cathedral ward here  you'll notice ariana is no longer in her  chair and it seems that there's  bloodstains on the ground head back to  the basement which is through the study  and you'll see that ariana is sitting in  another chair but with what appears to  be some type of baby monstrosity next to  her kill the baby to get another  umbilical board now return back to the  hunter's dream which is probably now  burning if you've killed Murr go next  consume three of the umbilical cords  after doing so enter the area where  gurmann is and refuse to give your life  up after defeating Kerman you'll queue  the ending you normally see except this  time somehow you deflect away the  monster trying to eat you  now we enter the fight with a moon  presence the alternate ending boss from  what I could tell you could easily avoid  his melee attacks it also uses its tail  to whip around and attack you as well as  burrowing it into the ground to get to  you from rank one of the most dangerous  moves the moon presence has is its eye  beam it seems to hit in a frontal cone  and will reduce your life to 1 HP but it  doesn't appear to kill you after this  move though there's a lot of downtime  for you to get in and attack and gain  that light back here's your chance to do  big damage to the boss  so get aggressive it appears that the  head and the hands might be the weak  points because that's what triggers  stagger State for me continue to dodge  the melee attacks and when the eye beam  comes make sure they either heal up  first or just go in attack and get your  life back  rinse and repeat and it should die now  you've earned yourself a secret  alternate ending  are you cold  oh good hunter what are your thoughts on  the ending was this the best ending  leave your comments below and stay tuned  to gain spot.com for more blood-borne  coverage  [Music]  you

